
INTRODUCTION
============

This bundle is the Trumpton Apps Accessible tools.

STARTING FROM SCRATCH (Linux)
=============================

Run these steps in order, from the AccessibleApps folder.

1. ./install-tools.sh

   Installs the compiler, Qt 6, GStreamer and other libraries needed to
   build every app (Debian / Ubuntu only), and selects Qt 6 as the default
   'qmake'.  It does not download the apps yet.

2. ./downloadapps-https.sh      (or ./downloadapps-ssh.sh if you use SSH keys)

   Clones EasyNotepad, ContactManager, ParseWeb, EncryptFolder, Lib,
   EncPad, GoogleFetch, KeyBackup and EasyList into this folder.

3. ./install-tools.sh --google-account

   Needed before ContactManager and GoogleFetch can be built.  Creates
   account-googleaccess.h in the ContactManager and GoogleFetch folders.
   If a header already has a Client ID and secret, it is kept and the
   script says so.  Otherwise the script asks for the Client ID and secret
   from your own Google Cloud project (one set is used for both) and
   explains how to create them.  The files are kept private and are
   git-ignored.

   To replace existing credentials, run ./install-tools.sh --newgoogleaccess
   instead.  Running install-tools.sh with no options does the same as
   --google-account, so you only need this step once.

4. ./dobuildlin.sh all

   Builds all the apps into the build folder, then copies the executables
   into the bin folder.

5. Run the programs from the bin folder, e.g. ./bin/ContactManager

To update the apps later, run ./pullupdates.sh, then ./dobuildlin.sh all
again.  You do not need to repeat steps 1 or 3 unless the Google
credentials change or a new package is required.

downloadapps-https.sh / downloadapps-ssh.sh
-------------------------------------------

This script downloads the applications from the 
git repository.

The tools should then be built as MSVC2019_64
applications using QT 6.7.3


pullupdates.sh
--------------

This script downloads any updates that have been
made to each application from the git repository.

Building Linux
--------------

To build, from a command line prompt, run dobuildlin.sh all.  This will build
the files into the build folder, then copy the executables into the bin
folder.  Libraries are not copied, and are expected to be available in the
standard lib folders.

Building Windows
----------------

If a new pull has been done, ensure that you remove the subdirectories 
under 'build' - this is because the version acquisition lines in the pro
files affect compiler switches, but do not 'dirty' the resulting makefiles.

To build, open a Visual C command line prompt, and run winshell.bat (this
will set all the required environment variables up). 

Then, to build, run dobuildwin.bat -  this will build the files into the 
build folder, then copy the executables into the bin folder, and copy 
across all of the relevant DLLs.

Deploying Windows
-----------------

Edit the deploy/config/config-win64-6.7.3.xml, and ensure that the
version number, and web repository location are correct.

The deployment assumes that Git has been installed.

Run deploywin.sh from a bash prompt - this will create the repository
installation files in the repository folder, using information from the
deploy folder.

Individual Package xml files for apps such as ContactManager are 
automatically created to include the version number from the appropriate 
version.h file.

If the dlls are updated (say through a change in the compiler libraries), 
the core package version in com.trumpton.base must be manually modified.

If the example files change, or the copyfiles app is modified, the 
examplefiles package (com.trumpton.base.exampleconfiguration) version 
must be manually changed.

Output Files will end up in 'repository'.  
The online files must be uploaded to vizier.

QT6 under Linux
===============

On Debian / Ubuntu, install-tools.sh (step 1 above) installs the Qt 6
packages and their dependencies.  Its package list is:

  build-essential git libssl-dev
  qt6-base-dev qt6-base-dev-tools qt6-5compat-dev qt6-multimedia-dev
  gstreamer1.0-plugins-base gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
  gstreamer1.0-libav gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio
  libspa-0.2-bluetooth clang

If you use Qt installed from the Qt online installer instead of apt, put
its qmake first on your PATH and install the same dependencies yourself.

